// Field Map page of the Dragon Quest III HD-2D Remake companion (Switch 1.1.0.0, build
// 4F41309B39EEBE5E): game data, the live location reader, the page values and the page art.
// Research contracts (research/dragon-quest-iii-hd-2d-remake): LOCATION.md, DUNGEON-FLOORS.md,
// runs/slice3-map/RESULT.md. Read-only: no guest writes, no guest calls.
//
// Game data (parsed at runtime from the player's own Nicola-Switch.pak, pins in dq3_map_pins.inc
// generated by research tools/dq3-map-pins.py):
//   GOP_MapList       row = current MapID (MAPLIST_*): NameTextID (the native Map title), MapImage
//                     (soft path -> a pinned texture), MapOriginalPos O / MapSize S (marker formula),
//                     PrefixId + MapFloorGroup + MapFloorSortNum (the floor selector), the day / night
//                     GOP_Map_SpotIcon rows and MapSpotIconIndex (interiors), IsUnderground.
//   GOP_Map_SpotIcon  12 entries {EMapSpotType, DispPosition (image px), display / hide progress}.
//   GOP_Hour          in-game hour -> EMapTimeFrame.
//   GOP_Text_Noun_ENGLISH  ListNoun of every TEXT_NOUN_ENGLISH_Map_* row (place / floor names).
//   en/GOP_Text_Map   Txt_Map_Menu_World_Map / _Alefgard_Map: the world map titles.
//
// Rules taken from the game's code (main-relative, 1.1.0):
//   0xbfa52c  town / dungeon marker: u = clamp((Y - O.y) * W / S.y, 0, W),
//             v = clamp(H - (X - O.x) * H / S.x, 0, H) on the W x H map image (X, Y sublevel-local).
//   0xbfa204  MapSpotIconIndex k != 0 (interiors that reuse the town image): the marker sits at spot
//             entry k (1-based) of the day / night spot row, PLAYER_SPOT_POS_Y_OFFSET lower unless
//             that entry is a HOUSE.
//   0xce4170  spot entries: row +0x124 (day) when GetMapTimeFrame != NIGHT (0xbe5db8), else +0x12c;
//             an entry shows when (display flag 0 or set) and not (hide flag set); the flags are
//             progress bits (0x877570: index <= 0xac, qword P + 0x1f0 + 8 * (i >> 6)).
//   0xce4130  GetFacilityIconIndex: type 1..14 -> float table main+0x490a108 (+15 for the map-sized
//             set the full map uses), HOUSE / NONE -> no icon. Cells of T_UI_Map_Facility_Icon_01
//             (5 x 6 cells of 88 px).
//   0xa2146c / 0xa213c8  MapTimeManager (world subsystem) float +0x30 = seconds:
//             hour = ((int)t % 86400) / 3600 -> GOP_Hour row HOUR_Hour%02d -> MapTimeFrame.
//   0xbfa518  the player icon angle = the root component world Yaw (clockwise, 0 = north).
//   0xbd96e8  the Map screen's time symbol: cell 1 (moon) when MapTimeFrame == NIGHT, else cell 0.
//   0xbd795c / 0xbd7bd0  world map extent: NicolaDataAssetCommon [G+0x4b8]: origin +0x168, tile
//             count (int) +0x170, tile size +0x178 (FIELD1); +0x180 / +0x188 / +0x190 underground.
//             The world image spans the extent: u = (Y - O.y) / (n.y * t.y) * W,
//             v = (1 - (X - O.x) / (n.x * t.x)) * H.
//   Visited maps P+0x250 (TArray<FName>) = the native floor selector's list (LOCATION.md §4).
//   Chests opened: the current map's *_SearchObj sublevel actors' SearchObjEventTrigger
//             (+0xF8 SearchObjEventGopId, +0x102 flag, +0x105 ESearchObjectType); IsTreasure
//             (0x845a00: type - 11 < 4, TREASURE_*); opened = bit `flag` of the P+0x128 bitset
//             (SetFlag 0x87aa3c with the trigger's +0x102 at 0x845958).
#pragma once

#include <array>
#include <cstdint>
#include <functional>
#include <map>
#include <memory>
#include <optional>
#include <span>
